.TH BIGFLOATCMPABS 3 "2026-09-21" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigFloatCmpAbs \- compare big float magnitudes exactly
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.sp
.BI "int bigFloatCmpAbs(const BigFloat *" "a" ","
.BI "    const BigFloat *" "b" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compares the absolute values of a and b, ignoring their signs.
Zero is less than every nonzero magnitude.
The comparison accounts for the exponent and mantissa bit length, then
compares aligned bits without shifting or truncating the inputs.
Equivalent values with different mantissa widths compare equal.
Normalized and unnormalized mantissas are supported; the size fields must
still be within the valid storage bounds.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \-1, 0, or 1 when the magnitude of a is less than, equal to, or
greater than that of b.  These values are comparison results, not errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bigFloatAdd (3),
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
